Third-party code inside the vendored bundles

Each file in this directory is an unmodified upstream distribution; VERSIONS
records versions, sources and checksums, and the LICENSE.* files hold each
library's own licence. Two bundles also contain code from other packages.
Their notices ship inside the minified files; mermaid.min.js carries most of
them in its "Bundled license information" comments.

mermaid.min.js (mermaid 12.0.0, MIT) bundles its dependencies, including:
- DOMPurify 3.4.12 (Apache-2.0 or MPL-2.0)
- chevrotain (Apache-2.0) and langium (MIT), through @mermaid-js/parser (MIT)
- cytoscape, cytoscape-cose-bilkent and cytoscape-fcose (MIT)
- d3 (ISC) and d3-sankey (BSD-3-Clause)
- lodash-es (MIT), dagre-d3-es (MIT), dayjs (MIT), KaTeX (MIT), khroma (MIT),
  marked (MIT), roughjs (MIT), stylis (MIT), uuid (MIT), es-toolkit (MIT),
  @braintree/sanitize-url (MIT), @iconify/utils (MIT), @upsetjs/venn.js (MIT)

force-graph.min.js (force-graph 1.51.4, MIT) bundles:
- d3-array, d3-drag, d3-scale, d3-scale-chromatic, d3-selection and d3-zoom
  (ISC), d3-force-3d (MIT)
- kapsule, accessor-fn, index-array-by, float-tooltip and
  canvas-color-tracker (MIT), bezier-js (MIT), lodash-es (MIT),
  @tweenjs/tween.js (MIT)
